{"request_sha256": "b280fd3e74f4ac1c49f0d35d7b4d323bfeab8b576601e5118d6562fabc893892", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "cab8b06e9f92fba201a63546092ac853c767927c057d5300e160c17b8047793a", "schema_sha256": "40b44f74e2832e0e52874cb964ff3f11b714cc6333ecca85f93378397c38d7cc", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 7363}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail"], "defects": ["crown-pinnate-arching-fronds: the render's crown is a near-flat radial starburst of short straight rachides; no frond arches outward-and-downward and no lower frond droops below the crown base, so the crown does not read as a palm rosette (defining mismatch against reference-0/reference-1, and against the owner's first priority).", "Frond length is a small fraction of trunk length (crown span ~250 px vs ~1000 px of visible trunk in the render), where reference-0 shows frond length a substantial fraction of trunk length and crown spread several times trunk width; the crown reads as a sparse tuft rather than a hemisphere/shuttlecock.", "Leaflets are rendered as sparse single-pixel-scale specks strung along bare rachides; the blade has no continuous margin, so the frond silhouette is skeletal rather than plumose (matches the owner's 'far too thin and short' note).", "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern: the rendered trunk surface is smooth and untextured over its whole length; the persistent leaf-base stub lattice of reference-1/reference-2 is not drawn. Owner-deferred (fn-110), but recorded as an unmet core reference trait, not dismissed.", "trunk-fibrous-matting: no fibre or husk is drawn anywhere on the rendered trunk. Owner-deferred (fn-110).", "fruit-clusters-pendent: no inflorescence or fruit bunch is drawn below the crown. Owner-deferred (fn-111).", "Trunk axis is wavy: an S-bend in the upper third plus a discrete kink/notch with a local diameter bulge around mid-height, against the owner's explicit 'straight or gently leaning, never wavy' requirement. The references' leaning/curving posture (trunk-lean-and-curve, variation) does not cover a local step discontinuity.", "Trunk diameter is not near-constant: it tapers continuously from a wide base to a markedly narrower apex, unlike the roughly columnar stems of reference-0/1/2.", "Finish quality against the fn9 spruce anchor: the crown foliage in the render is a thin scatter of isolated dark specks with visible gaps to sky throughout, below the anchor's dense, coherent foliage mass. Anchor cited for finish only, not morphology."], "observations": ["Only one render view (P-WHOLE, seed 1, render-0) was supplied; no P-TRUNK or P-BASE render exists, so close-range trunk and base cells cannot be read at reference resolution. The whole view does resolve that the trunk silhouette and shading are smooth along the full visible length, which is sufficient to state that no leaf-base or fibre structure is drawn at this scale.", "The render shows a single unbranched stem from ground to crown apex with no branches and no foliage attached anywhere along the trunk; the owner's 'nothing grows on the trunk' requirement is met, and the epiphytes of reference-1/2 (variation) are correctly absent.", "Frond count in the render is roughly 25-35 rachides radiating from one apical point, broadly within the inventory's 30-60 range for reference-0; the failure is in frond form and length, not in count or in the single-apex insertion.", "The render's foliage is a desaturated dark green-grey; reference-0 is deep saturated green and reference-1/2 pale grey-glaucous. This sits inside the recorded frond-colour-range variation and is not scored against the candidate.", "Specimen relationship across the three references is declared unknown and is treated as unknown here; no reference was assumed to show the same individual, and no cross-reference inference was made.", "reference-2 (P-BASE) does not in fact show the ground-level base; it is a close mid-trunk view. No reference resolves the root zone, so basal-flare remains weakly evidenced (reference-0 only, at distance).", "The render does show a modest basal widening where the trunk meets the ground, consistent in kind with the broad base visible in reference-0, though neither image resolves root-boss detail.", "The reviewer is Opus via the Claude adapter twins, uncalibrated on this model; this judgement is an attributed reading of the images, and the inventory statements were treated as interpretations rather than facts.", "No photorealism is required or assessed; all trait calls are at the level of recognisable structure at the catalogue finish floor."], "findings": [{"observation": "Every rachis in the render leaves the apex on a straight or very slightly curved line and terminates without recurving; the crown outline is a flat disc/starburst viewed against sky, not a rounded hemisphere, and no frond tip falls below the level of the crown insertion point.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with frond geometry lacking gravity-driven droop or an arch profile along the rachis, but no particular generator mechanism is established by the image."}, {"observation": "Frond length relative to trunk length and crown spread relative to trunk diameter are both far smaller in the render than in reference-0; leaflets appear as discrete specks rather than a continuous blade.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Matches the owner's stated first dials (leaflet size, frond length); the image alone does not identify which parameter dominates."}, {"observation": "Leaflet insertion pattern (grouping along the rachis, differing insertion angles, V-section/plumose cross-section, sharp rigid tips) cannot be read in the render: the drawn leaflets are at or near the resolution limit of the supplied P-WHOLE view.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The rendered trunk is smooth-shaded with no surface relief; no stub lattice and no fibrous matting are present at any height.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner states fn-110 trunk organs are not landed; the absence is scope-consistent, but it remains an unmet core reference trait rather than a pass."}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit bunch, stalk, or inflorescence is drawn below the crown in the render.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner states fn-111 date cluster is not landed; scope-consistent absence, still an unmet core trait."}, {"observation": "The rendered trunk is unbranched and single-stemmed from ground to crown, but its axis contains an S-bend and a discrete kink with a local bulge, and its diameter tapers substantially from base to apex.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Overall lean and curvature of a date palm trunk is itself within the reference range (strongly leaning S-curve in reference-0 vs vertical in reference-1/2), so lean alone is acceptable variation; what exceeds the range is the local step discontinuity in the render's mid-trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Render foliage colour is a desaturated dark green-grey, between the deep green of reference-0 and the grey-glaucous of reference-1/2.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Lighting, processing, maturity and cultivar are all candidate causes of the reference colour spread; none is established, so the render colour is not scored."}, {"observation": "No dead-frond skirt, no orange petiole-base sheath, and no basal leaflet spines are present in the render; all three are secondary traits in the inventory.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The render shows no smooth green crownshaft: fronds insert directly onto the trunk apex, agreeing with reference-1.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Foliage density in the render is well below the fn9 spruce anchor's coherent foliage mass at the same whole-tree framing; sky is visible through the crown across almost its entire area.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "anchor-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Anchor establishes finish floor only; the shortfall may be the same leaflet-size/frond-length deficit rather than an independent shading issue."}, {"observation": "Relative to the owner's framing this is a first rosette-only pass, so the trunk-organ and fruit gaps are expected; that does not make the crown readable as a palm rosette today.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Defining mismatch. The render has many rachides from a single apex (the one supported element), but they radiate as a flat starburst: no outward-and-downward arch, no recurve in the older/outer fronds, no frond tip below the crown base, and crown outline is a disc rather than a hemisphere/shuttlecock. Frond length is also a small fraction of trunk length against reference-0's substantial fraction."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Leaflets are drawn but only as sparse speck-scale marks on the rachis in the single P-WHOLE view; grouping, differing insertion angles, V-section and tip rigidity are not resolvable either way. Ambiguous evidence, so unknown rather than a downgrade; note the drawn leaflets are far smaller than reference scale, which is recorded as a defect but not converted into a pass or a fail for this trait."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The rendered trunk is smooth over its full visible length with no stub relief, no spiral, no rhomboid lattice, and no knobbly texture even at the distance scale where reference-0 shows it. Assessed on what is drawn, not invented. Owner-deferred to fn-110, which explains the gap but does not satisfy the trait."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No reddish-brown fibre or shredded husk is present anywhere on the rendered trunk; the surface is uniformly smooth shaded. Owner-deferred to fn-110."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Half supported, half mismatched, and the trait is compound. Single unbranched stem carrying the crown: supported, no branching anywhere. Roughly constant diameter: not met, the trunk tapers markedly from base to apex and carries a local bulge/notch at the mid-trunk kink. Combined with the wavy S-axis this is a defining departure from the columnar stems of all three references and from the owner's explicit straight-or-gently-leaning, near-constant-diameter requirement."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "No pendent bunch, stalk, or fruit mass is drawn below the crown. Owner-deferred to fn-111, so scope-consistent, but reported as an unmet core reference trait rather than dismissed. Evidence for the trait itself rests on reference-0 alone."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary, not a blocker. No collar of dead brown fronds below the living crown in the render; the upper trunk is bare. Optional refinement at this stage."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait. The render's desaturated dark green-grey foliage lies between the two observed reference states and is within acceptable variation; the reference spread itself is uncertain in cause, so no narrower target is imposed."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary, not a blocker. The render's crown apex is a plain dark mass with no pale green petioles and no rust-orange sheath patches. Optional refinement."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait, but the render falls outside the observed range rather than inside it. References span vertical-straight to a smooth strongly leaning S-curve; the render adds a discrete kink with a diameter step in the mid-trunk and a second reversal above it, giving a wavy rather than smoothly curved axis. Explicitly excluded by the owner ('never wavy')."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait, scene feature rather than species character. Absent from the render, as in reference-0, and the owner requires nothing on the trunk. Correct as drawn."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary. The render's trunk is a uniform warm dark grey-brown, within the stated grey-brown to reddish-brown range, but the trait is largely about stub-face versus fibre tonal differentiation, which cannot exist while no stubs are drawn. Unassessable in that respect."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary and itself uncertain in the inventory. The render shows a modest widening at ground contact, but at this framing neither the render nor reference-0 resolves root boss or offshoot detail, so a supported match cannot be claimed either way."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary, supported. No smooth green columnar sheath sits between crown and trunk in the render; frond bases attach directly to the trunk apex, as in reference-1."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary and uncertain in the references themselves. Proximal frond structure is not resolvable in the render at this scale; no call is possible."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Variation trait, but the render sits far outside any plausible reading of the range rather than inside it. Crown spread is roughly 2.5-3x the mid-trunk width and frond length is roughly a quarter of the visible trunk length, where reference-0 shows crown spread several times trunk width and frond length a substantial fraction of trunk length. The inventory's caveat that exact ratios cannot be measured is respected; the gap here is well beyond measurement error."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"717cf1e9-c4d3-40b7-a451-1df4ac7d9d3d","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename","ultrareview","security-review","usage-credits","extra-usage","usage","insights","recap","skill-doctor","goal","design-consent","design-revoke","list-agents","team-onboarding"],"terminal_slash_commands":["doctor","color","reload-plugins"],"apiKeySource":"none","claude_code_version":"2.1.278","output_style":"default","agents":["claude","Explore","general-purpose","Plan"],"skills":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator"],"plugins":[{"name":"flow-next","path":"/home/daniel/.claude-profiles/danithekiller93/plugins/cache/flow-next/flow-next/6.0.0","source":"flow-next@flow-next","version":"6.0.0"},{"name":"typesafe","path":"/home/daniel/.claude/plugins/cache/typesafe-ai/typesafe/0.5.7","source":"typesafe@typesafe-ai","version":"0.5.7"},{"name":"firecrawl","path":"/home/daniel/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-plugins-official/firecrawl/1.0.9","source":"firecra