ontinuously from a wide base to a markedly narrower apex, unlike the roughly columnar stems of reference-0/1/2.","Finish quality against the fn9 spruce anchor: the crown foliage in the render is a thin scatter of isolated dark specks with visible gaps to sky throughout, below the anchor's dense, coherent foliage mass. Anchor cited for finish only, not morphology."],"observations":["Only one render view (P-WHOLE, seed 1, render-0) was supplied; no P-TRUNK or P-BASE render exists, so close-range trunk and base cells cannot be read at reference resolution. The whole view does resolve that the trunk silhouette and shading are smooth along the full visible length, which is sufficient to state that no leaf-base or fibre structure is drawn at this scale.","The render shows a single unbranched stem from ground to crown apex with no branches and no foliage attached anywhere along the trunk; the owner's 'nothing grows on the trunk' requirement is met, and the epiphytes of reference-1/2 (variation) are correctly absent.","Frond count in the render is roughly 25-35 rachides radiating from one apical point, broadly within the inventory's 30-60 range for reference-0; the failure is in frond form and length, not in count or in the single-apex insertion.","The render's foliage is a desaturated dark green-grey; reference-0 is deep saturated green and reference-1/2 pale grey-glaucous. This sits inside the recorded frond-colour-range variation and is not scored against the candidate.","Specimen relationship across the three references is declared unknown and is treated as unknown here; no reference was assumed to show the same individual, and no cross-reference inference was made.","reference-2 (P-BASE) does not in fact show the ground-level base; it is a close mid-trunk view. No reference resolves the root zone, so basal-flare remains weakly evidenced (reference-0 only, at distance).","The render does show a modest basal widening where the trunk meets the ground, consistent in kind w